<sn><md>#### Deleting a Remote

Run:

```bash
rclone config
```

Choose:

```text
d) Delete remote
```

Then select the remote:

```text
gdrive
```

Rclone will ask for confirmation.

Deleting the remote **does not delete the files from Google Drive**.

It only removes the **Rclone configuration** that tells Rclone how to access that Drive.

```text
Rclone configuration
       │
       ├── gdrive ──────→ Google Drive
       │
       └── Delete gdrive
                │
                ▼
        Configuration removed
                │
                ▼
        Google Drive files remain
```
</md></sn><sn><md>#### Rename a Remote

You can also rename a remote:

```text
r) Rename remote
```

For example:

```text
gdrive:
```

can become:

```text
study:
```

The files remain unchanged; only the Rclone remote name changes.
</md></sn><sn><md>#### Copy a Remote

The:

```text
c) Copy remote
```

option creates another remote configuration based on an existing one.

For example:

```text
gdrive:
```

→

```text
gdrive-backup:
```

This can be useful when you want two Rclone remotes with similar configurations.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Quick Reference

| Action     | Menu option | Effect on cloud files |
| ---------- | ----------- | --------------------- |
| Edit       | `e`         | ❌ No deletion         |
| Delete     | `d`         | ❌ Files remain        |
| Rename     | `r`         | ❌ Files remain        |
| Copy       | `c`         | ❌ Files remain        |
| Create new | `n`         | ❌ No effect           |

**Important:** `rclone config` manages **connections/configurations**, while commands such as `rclone delete`, `rclone purge`, and `rclone sync` can actually modify or delete files on the remote.
</md></sn>